# Binaries
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.out
coverage.html

# Dependency directories
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# IDE and editor files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment files
.env
.env.local
*.local

# Database files (test artifacts). `*.db` alone is not enough: a scratch DB named
# `sqlite.db.tmp` matched none of these patterns and was committed at the module
# root, 221 KB of it, one commit after the CI guard for exactly this was added.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.tmp

# Build output
/dist/
bin/

# Track embedded UI assets (required for go:embed)
!ui/frontend/dist/

# Local-only frontend codegen convenience (lets `cd ui/frontend && buf generate`
# resolve ../proto). Not required to build: the TS client in src/lib/gen and the
# embedded dist are committed. Intentionally untracked.
ui/frontend/buf.yaml
ui/frontend/proto

# Compiled binaries from `go build ./...` at the repo root. This is a LIBRARY:
# a Go module zip contains every file under the module root, so a stray binary is
# downloaded by every `go get` and, because module versions are IMMUTABLE in the
# proxy, cannot be withdrawn afterwards. One slipped in this way and inflated the
# published zip 7.7x before it was caught.
/upgradematrix
/simple-durable-jobs
/sdj

# Hugo build output. Anchored to docs/ on purpose: a bare `public/` also matched
# ui/frontend/public/, which is Vite's static-asset directory and IS source --
# so the dashboard's favicon was silently excluded from the repo and reappeared
# missing in every clean build.
docs/public/
docs/resources/
.hugo_build.lock

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
bench-results/

# UI frontend
ui/frontend/node_modules/
ui/frontend/demo-dist/
docs/static/demo/

# Playwright
ui/frontend/playwright-report/
ui/frontend/test-results/

# Compiled binaries
/jobsui
ui/cmd/jobsui/jobsui
ui/cmd/e2etestserver/e2etestserver
e2etestserver
/chaostest
cmd/chaostest/chaostest
/sdj
